use std
into hair.amni

Imports: os, binary, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d. This file is a module with no main.

Struct `HairU` holds view_proj, view and proj (each `gfx::mat4`), then size, cam, to_sun, sun_rgb, hair, sky, params and look (each `float4`), then light_vp (`gfx::mat4`), light (`float4`) and shadow_vp (`gfx::mat4`), in that order, matching the GLSL uniform block `Hair` in shaders/strand_common.glsl.

Module state: `var on = false`, `var w = 0`, `var h = 0`, `var spc = 96`, `var points = 0`, `var segments = 0`, `var center = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `var bones = 0` (spring-bone count), `var bone_node int[>..]` (glTF node index of each bone, local to the asset), `var mats gfx::mat4[>..]` (one matrix per bone), and `var` handles `pts`, `rest`, `skin`, `matsb`, `segs`, `front`, `acc`, `lfront`, `lacc` (`gfx::Buffer`), `hairt` (`gfx::Texture`), `smp` (`gfx::Sampler`), `comp` (`gfx::Pipeline`), `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p`, `skin_p` (`gfx::ComputePipeline`, what `gfx::compute_pipeline` returns, assigned directly), each starting from `default<T>()`.

`hair_size(nw int, nh int)` sets w and h and (re)creates the screen-sized resources: with `rw = gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ`, `front = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 4, [])`, `acc = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 64, [])` and `hairt = gfx::texture(gfx::TextureDesc { format: gfx::RGBA16F, usage: gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COMPUTE_WRITE, width: nw as i32, height: nh as i32 })` (gfx::buffer always takes three arguments; an empty slice zero-fills).

`hair_open(path const byte[:], nw int, nh int, strands int) bool` reads the guides file with the unqualified `read_file(path, data)` into a `byte[>..]` (false: return false). Layout: 4 magic bytes, "HMG2" or "HMG3" (byte 3 is 50 or 51), then little-endian i32 guides, points, segments at bytes 4, 8, 12 (read with `binary::gather(data, at, 4) as int`), then points × 48 bytes, then segments × 16 bytes; an HMG3 file then has an i32 bone count `bones` at `e = 16 + points * 48 + segments * 16`, `bones` i32 node indices after it (append each to `bone_node`), then points × 16 bytes of skin data starting at `k = e + 4 + bones * 4`. Set `points`, `segments`, `spc = strands`; `pts = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `segs = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, segments * 16, <the segment bytes>)`. When `bones > 0`: `rest = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `skin = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 16, data[k..k + points * 16])`, resize `mats` to `bones` entries of `gfx::mat4_identity`, `matsb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, bones * 64, [])` and `skin_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_skin.comp"))`. `center` is the mean of the first three f32 of every point (point k at byte 16 + k*48, each `binary::f32_from_bits(binary::gather(data, at, 4) as! u32)`). Light buffers: `lfront = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 4, [])`, `lacc = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 64, [])`. `smp = gfx::sampler(gfx::NEAREST, gfx::CLAMP)`; `comp = gfx::pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.vert"), embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.frag"), gfx::PipelineDesc { blend: gfx::BLEND_PREMULTIPLIED })`; `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p` with `gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader(...))` of "shaders/strand_clear.comp", "shaders/strand_raster.comp", "shaders/strand_resolve.comp". Call `hair_size(nw, nh)`, set `on = true`, return true.

`hair_bone(i int) int` returns `bone_node[i]`, and `hair_pose(i int, m gfx::mat4)` sets `mats[i] = m` (a bone's motion, in the head's rest space) when `i` is in range.

`hair_draw(model gfx::mat4)` draws the strands (stored in the head's rest space) moved by `model`, onto `s3d::hdr_target()`; call it between `s3d::render_begin()` and `s3d::render_end(...)`. Return when `!on`. Let `im = linalg::inverse(model)`. Fill `var u = default<HairU>()`: view_proj `gfx::mul(s3d::view_proj_nj, model)`, view `gfx::mul(s3d::view_mat, model)`, proj `s3d::proj_mat`; size (w, h, spc, segments, all `as f32`); cam: `e = linalg::point(im, s3d::view.eye)` as (e.x, e.y, e.z, 0.7); to_sun: `t = gfx::mul(im, float4 { s3d::sun.to_sun.x, s3d::sun.to_sun.y, s3d::sun.to_sun.z, 0.0 })`, `ld = linalg::unit3(float3 { t.x, t.y, t.z })`, stored as (ld, 0); sun_rgb `s3d::sun.rgb` with w 0; hair (0.58, 0.38, 0.14, 0.42); sky (0.12, 0.13, 0.15, 40.0); params (0.004, 1.7, 0.004, 0.00007); look (1.0, 6.0, 0.0, 0.7); light_vp `gfx::mul(gfx::perspective(0.24, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0), gfx::look_at(center + ld * 3.0, center, float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }))`; light (512, 512, 0.35, 256 / tan(0.12)) all `as f32`; shadow_vp `gfx::mul(s3d::cascade_vp[0], model)`. Each compute pass: `gfx::begin_compute(...)`, `gfx::bind(pipeline)`, set `u.look.z` to the mode, `gfx::uniforms(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, u)`, ..., `gfx::end_compute()`. A nested `fn raster(rw0 gfx::Buffer, rw1 gfx::Buffer, ro0 gfx::Buffer, ro1 gfx::Buffer, mode int)` runs one raster pass: read-write [rw0, rw1], raster_p, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, s3d::nd_target(), smp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 1, s3d::shadow_map, smp)`, storage buffers 0..3 = pts, segs, ro0, ro1, dispatch ((segments + 63) / 64, spc, 1). Order: first, when `bones > 0`, skin the strands: `gfx::update_buffer(matsb, 0, bytes_of(mats)[..bones * 64])`, then a compute pass with read-write buffers [pts], skin_p, `u.size.w = points as f32` before its `gfx::uniforms`, storage buffers 0..2 = rest, skin, matsb, dispatch ((points + 63) / 64, 1, 1), and set `u.size.w = segments as f32` back after it; then clear [front, acc] mode 0 dispatching ((w*h + 63) / 64, 1, 1); clear [lfront, lacc] mode 2 dispatching ((512*512 + 63) / 64, 1, 1); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 2); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 3); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 0); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 1); resolve with buffers [] and textures [hairt] (two-list `gfx::begin_compute`), resolve_p, mode 1, storage buffer 0 = acc, dispatch ((w + 7) / 8, (h + 7) / 8, 1); then `if gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [s3d::hdr_target(), gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}], clear_color: false, .. })` { `gfx::bind(comp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::FRAGMENT, 0, hairt, smp)`, `gfx::draw(3)`, `gfx::end_pass()` }.
